"delivery.podContainsFullAddress","KEY","truth",NULL,"DOCUMENT","CARRIER_PROOF_OF_DELIVERY","Does the proof of delivery contain the full delivery address, as 11.10.2.6 requires?",NULL,"SECTION 7.11.1, AND THE KEY THAT MAKES THIS CONDITION AUTOMATABLE. The obvious framing - delivery.recipientAddress, the address itself - is a claim about the WORLD that nothing this platform holds could contradict, so it could never decide a ground. But the rulebook is not asking us to verify the address belongs to the Cardholder; the ISSUER does that. It is stating what counts as evidence. So the fact is about the DOCUMENT - does this record contain a full address - which is true on its own face, SELF_CONTAINED, and decides. A PARTIAL address makes this FALSE: 11.10.2.6 says tracking with a partial address is not permitted, so the shortfall is reported rather than hidden.
