"credit.settledBeforeDispute","KEY","truth",NULL,"SYSTEM",NULL,"Had the credit already settled when the Issuer raised the Dispute?","PARTIAL, and ACCEPTED - see sanction. The passage asks whether the credit was 'not addressed by the Issuer in the Dispute', a statement about the Issuer's own handling that no system of record here holds. What is held is the ordering: a credit that had settled before the Dispute was raised was there to be addressed, and the Issuer disputed the amount regardless.","It cannot distinguish an Issuer that overlooked the credit from one that considered it and disputed anyway - both are 'not addressed' on the face of the record, and the second is a position the Issuer is entitled to take. That is the residual risk in contesting on this key, and it is the reason it needs SME sign-off rather than acceptance because the arithmetic works.
SOURCE: Credit.creditDate <= Dispute.reportedDate
APPROVAL LICENSED: ANY_OF( ALL_OF(credit.exists, credit.coversDisputed, credit.settledBeforeDispute), ALL_OF(reversal.exists, reversal.settledBeforeDispute) )
APPROVAL SCOPE: A credit or Reversal issued by the Merchant was not addressed by the Issuer in the Dispute.
RESIDUAL RISK: TWO RISKS, and the second is the larger. (1) Neither branch can distinguish an Issuer that OVERLOOKED the credit or Reversal from one that CONSIDERED it and disputed anyway - both look identical on the settlement record, and the second is a position the Issuer is entitled to take. (2) The REVERSAL branch has NO coverage test. The credit branch requires credit.coversDisputed; no reversal amount is held, so a Reversal of any size - a partial reversal of a fraction of the Transaction - satisfies this ground exactly as a full one does. That is a materially weaker argument than the credit branch and will file some representments an Issuer can rebut on the amount alone. Closing it needs the reversal amount sourced, not a change here. Until then, the loss rate on the reversal branch is worth measuring SEPARATELY from the credit branch - they are one ground in the rulebook and two different bets in practice.
CONFIRMED 2026-08-09, POC SCOPE ONLY. Confirmed against an SME_APPROVED estate signed the same day for the POC. The reading is not settled by a scheme subject matter expert and one must rule before any production filing; nothing here reaches a card network. The same scope is recorded on artifact.sanction.confirmation_notes.
APPROVAL RECORD (verbatim): Ram, Architect. SANCTION S-001, accepted 2026-08-06. STATUS: INTERIM - pending SME confirmation at first sign-off. This is not a settled reading of the rulebook. Accepted because without it the principal ground on four conditions (13.1, 13.5, 13.6, 13.7) is permanently undecidable, and the alternative is not a better predicate but no automation. TWO CONDITIONS ATTACH: (1) AUTO_SUBMIT is not permitted on any ground resting on this sanction - cap at ASSEMBLE_REVIEW until an SME confirms the reading; (2) the interim status travels into every review packet, so an SME reading any of the four conditions sees that this was accepted to unblock the build rather than settled.
STATUS: CONFIRMED
CONFIRMED: Ram, Architect 2026-08-09
WAS CONFIRMED (auto-submit) BY: Ram, Architect 2026-08-09",NULL
